{
  "title": "UniformStruct",
  "description": "A struct nested inside a uniform block. A nested struct is a group of fields within the containing block, not a second GPU resource: it shares the block's buffer and its revision. Declaring one explicitly - rather than treating any plain object as a struct - is what keeps `{ type, default }` metadata distinguishable from a group of fields.",
